% ============================================================================
% wordgenx syntax tour (language design v0.2)
% Every construct of the language in one file. The test suite parses this file
% and requires zero diagnostics.
% ============================================================================

\document[template="templates/corporate.dotx", lang=en-GB, smart-quotes=on]

\meta[
  title    = "Syntax Tour",
  author   = "wordgenx contributors",
  keywords = (docx, markup),
  custom.project-code = "WX-001",   % custom document property
]

\settings[even-odd-headers, update-fields-on-open=on, protection=(mode=forms, enforce)]
\use{styles/house.wgxs}
\use{std:callout}

\section[size=A4, margins=(top=2.5cm, bottom=2.5cm, inside=3cm, outside=2cm), mirror, title-page]
\header[first]{}
\header{\field{STYLEREF "Heading 1" \n} \tab \field{TITLE}}
\footer{\align[center]{Page \pagenum of \numpages}}

\let{product}{wordgenx Compiler}

\define{callout}[title="Key takeaway", id]{
  \table[style="Callout", widths=(1fr), id=#id]{\row{\cell{
    \p[style="Callout Title"]{#title}

    #body
  }}}
}

\toc[levels=1-3, title="Contents"]

= Introduction {#sec:intro}

Plain prose needs no markup. Revenue grew 12% to $48.2M; about 5% of that is
currency effects. The \product is *strong*, _emphasised_, `code`, or both:
*very _important_*. Escapes: \* \_ \% \{ \} \\ and a non-breaking~space.
snake_case_name and 5 * 3 need no escapes, and neither does jane@example.com.

See @sec:details, \ref[form=text]{sec:intro} or [the website](https://example.com)
and <https://example.org/docs?a=1&b=2>. A footnote.\footnote{With *markup* inside.}

Inline math: \m{e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0}, and a literal \#{ is escaped.

== Lists {#sec:details}

- First bullet
- Second bullet, which continues
  on the next line
  - nested bullet
1. Numbered
2. Numbered, with a nested lettered list
   a. lettered
   b. lettered

\list[MSA]{
1. {#cl:term} Term
   1. This Agreement commences on the Effective Date.
2. {#cl:charges} Charges and Payment
   1. {#cl:invoice} The Supplier shall invoice monthly.
   2. If any sum is not paid when due, the Supplier may:
      a. charge interest; and
      b. suspend the Services, provided that clause @cl:invoice has been complied with.
}

=* Unnumbered heading

\caption[Table, id=tbl:rev]{Quarterly revenue}
\table[style="Data Grid", header-rows=1, widths=(4cm, 1fr, 1fr), columns=(left, decimal, decimal)]{
  | Item     | Q1    | Q2    |
  | Revenue  | 10.5  | 12.25 |
  | Cost     | \cell[shade=#FFF2CC]{7} | `a|b` |
  | \cell[colspan=3, align=center]{*Total: 7*} |||
}

\table[widths=(1fr, 2fr)]{
  \row[header, height=(1cm, exact)]{ \cell{Name} \cell{Description} }
  \row{
    \cell[rowspan=2, valign=center]{Merged}
    \cell{
      First paragraph.

      - a list inside a cell
    }
  }
  \row{ \cell{Second row, right column} }   % the left cell is covered by the rowspan
}

\figure[id=fig:arch, width=12cm, align=center]{
  \image{img/architecture_v2%20final.png}
  \caption{Overall architecture}
}

$$ \int_0^\infty e^{-x^2}\,dx = \frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2} $$ {#eq:gauss}

$$\begin{aligned}
  a &= b + c \\
    &= d
\end{aligned}$$ {#eq:chain}

```python {#lst:hello, caption="Hello world", line-numbers}
def hello():
    print("hi {there}")   # braces and \backslashes are verbatim
```

\callout[title="Mind the gap"]{Volume growth is outpacing hub capacity.}

\comment[author="R. Patel", text={Rich comment with *markup*.}]{thirty (30) days}
\control[type=dropdown, tag=status, items=("Draft", "Final")]{Draft}
\font[color=theme.accent1.darker(25%), size=10pt]{Theme colours}

\tabs[(8cm, center), (16cm, right, leader=dot)]{Left\tab Centered\tab Right}

\p[style="Body Text", align=center, space-before=12pt, keep-with-next]{A paragraph with options.}

\section[orientation=landscape, break=next-page]

\date[kind=fixed, format="d MMMM yyyy"]
